# OpenRiC Workspace - the demonstration's nightly reset (after Heratio's heratio-demo-reset).
# At 02:00, when few visit, the fixed baseline is put back, undoing whatever visitors changed since it was taken.
# The baseline is fixed: take a new one by hand only when the demonstration data is deliberately changed (a recording
# session, new showcase content, a release): sudo -u www-data bin/demo-snapshot. Dr Johan Pieterse, 16 November 2026,
# replacing the daily 16:00 snapshot of 10 November, which kept every visitor's change made before 16:00, the learners'
# exercises and capstones of Archives from the Ground Up among them. Times are the server's (Africa/Johannesburg).
# Only for a demonstration: bin/demo-reset refuses unless WORKSPACE_DEMO_EMAIL is set. Install as root:
#   cp deploy/cron/openric-workspace-demo-reset /etc/cron.d/ && chmod 0644 /etc/cron.d/openric-workspace-demo-reset
# and take the first baseline: sudo -u www-data bin/demo-snapshot.
# Copyright (C) 2026 Johan Pieterse / Plain Sailing Information Systems
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
MAILTO=""

0 2 * * * root /usr/share/nginx/openric-workspace-live/bin/demo-reset >> /usr/share/nginx/openric-workspace-live/storage/logs/demo-reset.log 2>&1
